00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.360
But the question was with
buzzwords like ChatGPT,

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:02.780
has AI impacted your
workflow as of now?

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:03.800
Yeah.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:08.780
Specifically with
the ChatGPT, we

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.720
started using in a
limited way, to be frank.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:16.040
There's a lot of great
stuff about that technology

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:18.540
and that tool specifically.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:23.110
There's a lot of things
that we need to make sure,

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:26.570
like privacy,
security, making sure

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.760
that it's used
appropriately, and we

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:33.929
don't raise the-- or data,
or secret sauce, the code.

00:08:33.929 --> 00:08:39.530
So we have used it like we use
Google, and Stack Overflow,

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:42.799
and the many other tools
that are out there.

00:08:42.799 --> 00:08:47.460
So I want to make
sure that-- or we

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:52.230
want to make sure that
we do it in a meaningful

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.110
but educated way.

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:57.120
So we've been trying to--

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.810
we released some statements
about what is it, how

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.060
to use it, where not to use it.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:08.530
And but definitely evaluating
what is coming in the future.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:09.690
I think there is a--

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:13.470
AI in general has impacted
your workflow absolutely.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:16.560
We started doing AI
and machine learning

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.330
models over 10 years ago.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:20.880
Like probably a lot
of the big companies,

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:25.200
we have a lot of
models in production

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.900
provided producing results.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:31.020
We have a patented
model factor in play

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:34.780
when we have all the
AI models implemented.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.390
So there are many,
many different ways

00:09:36.390 --> 00:09:41.160
that we use them from
underwriting, pricing, claims,

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.180
acquisition, you name it.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.930
So we can always get
into any specific detail.

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:52.230
But definitely it's one of
the many ways we use it.

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:57.700
Thank you.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.560
I just wanted to
